design eature_descriptions\F_173_token_count.md:14:during a release, the token count began to change up and down like crazy. clear indication that something is going wrong during the calculation of the token usage.
design eature_descriptions\F_173_token_count.md:18:token usage of released cards is no longer going to change. we can keep the summaries for these cards in more convenient places, like in a project wide json file for instance.
designeleases\0_0_3elease_notes.md:22:- See Codex reasoning, commands, tool activity, and account limits.
design eature_descriptions\F_186_action_popup_bottom_of_chat_log.md:28:For Codex, `agent_streaming_adapter.js` receives `thread/tokenUsage/updated` during a turn and immediately emits live cumulative token usage. It retains `contextWindowUsage` until `turn/completed`, however. Only then does `agent_streaming_event_handlers.js` publish that snapshot to live `AgentConversation` state. Context percentage therefore updates after the turn, despite provider data arriving earlier.
design eature_descriptions\F_186_action_popup_bottom_of_chat_log.md:30:Here, **chatlog** means scrollable transcript viewport. **Metadata row** means row containing status, duration, and context usage. **Available** means a valid `thread/tokenUsage/updated` notification has been received; turn completion is not required.
design eature_descriptions\F_186_action_popup_bottom_of_chat_log.md:36:- Include latest valid `contextWindowUsage` in each Codex streaming `usage` event. In live usage handler, forward snapshot with cumulative token usage through existing action-run `agentUsage` update path so `ActionRunRegistry` immutably updates displayed conversation during active turn.
design eature_descriptions\F_186_action_popup_bottom_of_chat_log.md:45:- First valid Codex `thread/tokenUsage/updated` notification updates displayed context percentage before `turn/completed`, agent shutdown, popup reopen, or project reload.
designeleases\0_0_3\F_86_codex_conversation_activity_frontend.md:17:Show Codex reasoning, commands, and other useful agent activity in the conversation chat, and show current Codex account limits in the application status bar.
designeleases\0_0_3\F_86_codex_conversation_activity_frontend.md:23:Live action state in `ActionExecutionService` holds user messages plus one assistant text buffer. It cannot carry item lifecycle updates. `StatusBar` contains project counts, sync, persisted token usage, remote status, keyboard state, and running agents. No service or component consumes Codex account limits.
designeleases\0_0_3\F_86_codex_conversation_activity_frontend.md:45:- Add a runtime `CodexRateLimitService` owning the current in-memory snapshot and bridge subscription. This is application state; `StatusBar` and other components do not own it.
designeleases\0_0_3\F_86_codex_conversation_activity_frontend.md:47:- Add `CodexRateLimitStatus` as a separate leaf component in `StatusBar`. Subscribe inside this smallest component.
designeleases\0_0_3\F_86_codex_conversation_activity_frontend.md:84:- Add `CodexRateLimitService` tests for subscription, replacement, staleness, reconnect, and no persistence.
designeleases\0_0_3\F_85_codex_app_server_activity_backend.md:26:- `account/rateLimits/updated` is ignored. Existing token usage is per conversation and persisted; it is a different concept.
designeleases\0_0_3\F_85_codex_app_server_activity_backend.md:60:- Handle `account/rateLimits/updated` separately from run events. Also issue `account/rateLimits/read` after initialization so the status bar need not wait for a later change.
designeleases\0_0_3\F_85_codex_app_server_activity_backend.md:61:- Normalize the single-bucket and `rateLimitsByLimitId` forms into an array keyed by `limitId`. Preserve `limitName`, primary/secondary windows, used percent, reset time, plan type, reached type, credit summary, and observation time.
designeleases\0_0_3\F_85_codex_app_server_activity_backend.md:97:- Existing changed-path collection, token usage, interactive questions, turn lifecycle, and provider continuation still work.
designeleases\0_0_3\F_85_codex_app_server_activity_backend.md:105:- [F_054 agent token usage tracking](../releases/0_0_2/F_054_agent_token_usage_tracking.md)
design eature_descriptions\F_194_track_token_usage_vs_usage_metrics.md:5:title: track token usage vs usage metrics
design eature_descriptions\F_194_track_token_usage_vs_usage_metrics.md:17:we also report 'account limits'. currently already working for codex, soon for claude likely too (see [F\_193\_report\_claude\_usage\_quotas.md](design/feature_descriptions/F_193_report_claude_usage_quotas.md) )
design eature_descriptions\F_194_track_token_usage_vs_usage_metrics.md:19:now we want to measure and save both values (deltas) over time so we can track: how many tokens were used per hour, per day, per week and how much account limits shrank in the same period, so how much account usage there was.
design eature_descriptions\F_194_track_token_usage_vs_usage_metrics.md:21:This allows us to check how the relationship is between token usage and account usage at various hours and days.
design eature_descriptions\F_193_report_claude_usage_quotas.md:18:we are already reporting usage limits for codex in the apps status bar. we need to provide similar information from the claude cli.
design eature_descriptions\F_193_report_claude_usage_quotas.md:51:* `CodexStreamingAdapter` (`desktop/src/actions/agent/agent_streaming_adapter.js`) reads rate limits from the codex app-server: `account/rateLimits/read` reply plus `account/rateLimits/updated` notifications. It calls `onRuntimeEvent({ kind, observedAt, payload })`.
design eature_descriptions\F_193_report_claude_usage_quotas.md:54:* Renderer `CodexRateLimitService` (`app/src/services/agents/codex_rate_limit_service.ts`) holds `{ receivedAt, snapshot, stale }`, schedules a "stale" flip at the earliest `resetsAt`. "Stale" = reset time passed, old numbers no longer trusted.
design eature_descriptions\F_193_report_claude_usage_quotas.md:55:* UI: `CodexRateLimitStatus` (status-bar button) + `CodexRateLimitDetails` (popover), driven by `codexRateLimitPresentation`. Mounted in `status_bar.tsx` (desktop) and `mobile_project_status.tsx` (mobile). Shows "Codex N% used", warns at 80%, error at 100%/reached.
design eature_descriptions\F_193_report_claude_usage_quotas.md:61:Ship a **separate claude indicator** (not merged into codex). "Separate indicator" = its own status-bar control + service, sitting next to `CodexRateLimitStatus`, claude-specific wording and fields.
design eature_descriptions\F_193_report_claude_usage_quotas.md:70:* Add a `ClaudeRuntimeService` (`desktop/src/actions/agent/claude_runtime_service.js`), modeled on `CodexRuntimeService`: validate/normalize the parsed snapshot, hold one account-wide claude snapshot, emit a `rateLimits` event, expose `getSnapshot`/`subscribe`, guard against out-of-order `observedAt` (older observation ignored). Do not republish an unchanged snapshot (respect granular-events rule).
design eature_descriptions\F_193_report_claude_usage_quotas.md:76:* New preload bridge `window.md2ClaudeRuntime` (`desktop/src/shell/preload.js` + `local_bridge_dispatch.js` + `main.js`), mirroring the codex runtime bridge: `getClaudeRateLimits()`, `onClaudeRateLimits(cb)`, `onConnectionChanged?`. New typed interface `app/src/data/electron_claude_runtime_bridge.ts` with a `ClaudeRateLimitSnapshot` type matching the Phase 1 shape.
design eature_descriptions\F_193_report_claude_usage_quotas.md:80:* `ClaudeRateLimitService` (`app/src/services/agents/claude_rate_limit_service.ts`), mirror of `CodexRateLimitService`: `{ receivedAt, snapshot, stale }`, subscribe to bridge, schedule stale flip at earliest `resetsAt`, `EventTarget` `changed` event, `register('claudeRateLimitService', this)`.
design eature_descriptions\F_193_report_claude_usage_quotas.md:82:* New `ClaudeRateLimitStatus` + `ClaudeRateLimitDetails` components (do **not** overload the codex ones). Label shows "Claude N% used" like codex; popover lists session + weekly rows with reset times.
design eature_descriptions\F_193_report_claude_usage_quotas.md:83:* Mount the new component next to `CodexRateLimitStatus` in `status_bar.tsx` and `mobile_project_status.tsx`. Render nothing when no claude snapshot / stale (same null-render discipline as codex).
