2_open_github_repository_from_electron.md:13:When the react app is running in the electron environment, it defaults to opening projects by selecting a folder.\ndesign\\feature_descriptions\\F_152_open_github_repository_from_electron.md:20:We need to add an 'open dialog' to support this feature. from this dialog, the user can always choose between personal or public repository, and when running in the electron environment, the user can also select a folder.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\B_101_action_agent_selectors_forget_settings.md:15:when you close and re-open an action popup, the selected agent configuration is lost and appears to go back to default.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\B_101_action_agent_selectors_forget_settings.md:19:`ActionPopupContent` creates a new `ActionRunInputStore` for each action/context mount. Selector changes update that store, but closing the popup destroys it. Reopening creates an empty snapshot, so `useActionRunSettings` resolves agent, model, thinking level, access level, and approval policy from the action definition and desktop defaults again.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\B_101_action_agent_selectors_forget_settings.md:46:* Project, folder, and regular-file action popups keep current session-only selector behavior.\napp\\src\\theme\\theme_provider.tsx:18: * Electron main process when running on the desktop.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\B_100_claude_agent_shows_all_responses_double.md:13:When an action is run by the claude agent, all responses, accept the last one he gives are shown 2 times in the chatlog. so 2 identical bubbles below each other.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\B_100_claude_agent_shows_all_responses_double.md:42:* Running a Claude action produces exactly one chatlog bubble per assistant step; no step (except formerly the last) is duplicated.\ndesign\\architecture\\initial description\\animations.md:6:to indicate that long running actions are busy (and we don't know how long they will run), animations can be used.\ndesign\\architecture\\initial description\\action_popup.md:13:- While the action is running, `Cancel` asks Electron to stop the active process and chain.\ndesign\\architecture\\initial description\\actions.md:74:- Activating an entry point opens the action popup for the action `id` and selected context.\ndesign\\actions\\prepare-project.json:10:  \"prompt\": \"Your task is to prepare this project for development.\\n\\nInstructions:\\n\\n1. Start by locating and reading the \\\\`README.md\\\\` file in the current directory.\\n2. Follow the setup instructions in that README exactly.\\n3. If the main README refers to additional \\\\`README.md\\\\` files in subdirectories, or if subdirectories contain setup instructions that are required for development, read those as well.\\n4. Perform all necessary project setup steps, including (where applicable):\\n   1. Installing dependencies.\\n   2. Installing toolchains or SDKs.\\n   3. Restoring packages.\\n   4. Creating generated files.\\n   5. Running bootstrap or setup scripts.\\n   6. Initializing git submodules.\\n   7. Installing workspace/package manager dependencies.\\n   8. Building any required generated artifacts.\\n5. Do not start long-running processes such as development servers or watch tasks unless the README explicitly requires them as part of setup.\\n6. If any step requires user input, elevated privileges, secrets, credentials, or external configuration, stop and explain exactly what is needed before proceeding.\\n7. If multiple package managers or setup methods are available, use the one recommended by the project's documentation.\\n8. If the documentation contains conflicting instructions, prefer the instructions in the top-level \\\\`README.md\\\\` and explain any conflict.\\n9. When setup is complete, provide a concise summary including:\\n   1. The steps that were performed.\\n   2. Any issues or warnings encountered.\\n   3. Any manual steps the developer still needs to complete.\\n   4. Whether the project appears ready for development.\\n\\nDo not make assumptions beyond what is documented. Base your actions on the project's documentation whenever possible.\\nYou do not need to run linting or tests after a fresh install.\\nBe brief, but never compress away the subject, timing, or causal chain. Define ambiguous technical phrases. use $caveman skill\"\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\release_notes.md:13:- Enjoy faster, more stable action popups and conversations.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\release_notes.md:19:- Keep completed reasoning blocks out of conversation history.\ndesign\\architecture\\current_model_react.md:13:├─ runningAgents: RunningAgent[]\r\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_025_move_action_popup_state_to_leaf_owners.md:5:title: move action popup state and subscriptions to leaf owners\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_025_move_action_popup_state_to_leaf_owners.md:30:- Remove `useActionPopupController`; do not replace it with another aggregate controller.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_025_move_action_popup_state_to_leaf_owners.md:31:- Remove active-run subscriptions from `ActionPopup` and `ActionPopupContent`.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_025_move_action_popup_state_to_leaf_owners.md:53:- Add render-count regression tests around `ActionPopup` and `ActionPopupContent`.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_025_move_action_popup_state_to_leaf_owners.md:62:- [ ] `useActionPopupController` is deleted.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_024_replace_execution_state_with_scoped_action_runs.md:70:- Global running indicators may subscribe to the active-run aggregate.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_023_use_one_agent_conversation_model.md:27:J-020 unified conversation content into `entries`, but renderer run state still stores `LiveAgentTurn`. `useActionPopupController` converts that object into a new `AgentConversation` during rendering. This duplicates models, metadata, and ownership.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_022_stabilize_action_prompt_drafts.md:23:Give each action prompt draft one lifetime-stable external store. Typing, flushing, preparing, replacing, clearing, restoring, and remotely synchronizing a prompt must not place the prompt text or reset counters in `ActionPopupContent` or its controller React state.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_022_stabilize_action_prompt_drafts.md:31:- `useActionPopupController` stores prompt value, preparation status, and reset token in React state.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_022_stabilize_action_prompt_drafts.md:32:- `ActionPopupContent` creates a new `ActionPromptDraft` whenever the controller prompt or reset token changes.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_022_stabilize_action_prompt_drafts.md:58:- `ActionPopupContent` obtains or receives the stable draft store but does not subscribe to its value or preparation state.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_022_stabilize_action_prompt_drafts.md:59:- `useActionPopupController` removes `promptState`, `promptResetToken`, prompt-value derivation, and `handlePromptChange` state updates.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_022_stabilize_action_prompt_drafts.md:61:- `ActionPopupBottomRow` remains the narrow subscriber for live prompt-dependent button state.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_022_stabilize_action_prompt_drafts.md:68:- Normal typing does not render `ActionPopupContent`, the popup controller owner, or unrelated popup sections.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_022_stabilize_action_prompt_drafts.md:82:- Popup regression tests count renders and prove repeated typing and flushes do not render `ActionPopupContent`.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_022_stabilize_action_prompt_drafts.md:91:- [ ] Typing and flushing do not render `ActionPopupContent` or its controller owner.\ndesign\\architecture\\initial description\\app layout.md:24:    - number of running agents (with list in popup)?\r\ndesign\\architecture\\initial description\\app layout.md:35:  - led indicator for logs / currently running agents/actions?\r\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\release_notes.md:14:- Open action popups full-screen by default on mobile.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\release_notes.md:16:- View grouped tool calls in a cleaner conversation box.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\release_notes.md:36:- Merge-conflict agents now open in the standard action popup.\ndesign\\architecture\\initial description\\overview.md:56:- when app is running in Electron, allow running shell commands to start an agent.\r\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_020_unify_agent_conversation_entries.md:35:- **Event entry**: reasoning, tool use, command execution, diagnostics, failures, and lifecycle observations.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\J_020_unify_agent_conversation_entries.md:114:- Completed reasoning events may still be hidden by chat presentation rules, but filtering cannot reorder remaining entries.\ndesktop\\src\\integrations\\remote_control_service.test.mjs:43:        const actionEvent = { runId: 'action-1', sequence: 1, status: 'running', type: 'run' };\ndesign\\architecture\\initial description\\timers.md:8:  - the user selects a date and time on the action popup\ndesign\\architecture\\initial description\\timers.md:11:- on the action popup, \"Schedule\" button, in front of the Run button\r\ndesign\\architecture\\initial description\\timers.md:15:    - check if there are any scheduled actions; if so, start running the timer\r\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\F_98_worktree_vs_project_folder_placeholders.md:13:We have 'rootProjectFolder' placeholder. this currently maps to the folder that the agent is running on, so it could the the main project folder or a worktree.&#x20;\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\F_98_worktree_vs_project_folder_placeholders.md:15:We need to improve this and split it up in `worktree-folder` and 'project-folder' where the last one always references the main project folder while 'worktree-folder' references the folder that the agent is currently running in.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\F_166_improve_input_and_bottom_row_on_action_popup.md:5:title: Improve input and bottom row on action popup\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\F_166_improve_input_and_bottom_row_on_action_popup.md:15:We need to improve layout and position of input and bottom row. The goal is to provide as much viewing area as possible to the chatlog while providing optimal input size while editing a prompt.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\F_166_improve_input_and_bottom_row_on_action_popup.md:25:`ActionAgentPrompt` renders a fixed-height prompt surface below the conversation. Its horizontal resize bar is always enabled. Prompt height starts from `md2.actionPromptHeight`, or 140 px when no saved height exists, and remains unchanged when the prompt becomes empty. The prompt therefore reserves the same chatlog space whether it contains many lines or no text.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\F_166_improve_input_and_bottom_row_on_action_popup.md:27:`ActionPopupBottomRow` is a separate popup footer after the scroll body. It uses `background.default`, a top border, and popup-wide padding, which creates the gray bar below the prompt. It owns usage information and Finish, Schedule, Send, Run, and Stop controls. Command actions have no visible prompt surface, so their Run row must remain standalone.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\F_166_improve_input_and_bottom_row_on_action_popup.md:32:- Make the prompt surface a column with three regions: scrollable editor, optional predefined phrases, and `ActionPopupBottomRow` as a non-scrolling footer. Sticky means the footer remains visible at the surface bottom while editor content scrolls; it does not require CSS `position: sticky`.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\F_166_improve_input_and_bottom_row_on_action_popup.md:38:- Subscribe to prompt text at the smallest component that changes prompt height or resize availability. Do not hoist draft updates into `ActionPopupContent`, because chatlog and unrelated popup content must not rerender for each keystroke.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\F_166_improve_input_and_bottom_row_on_action_popup.md:43:- Given an empty or whitespace-only agent prompt, its editable region is one line high and the chatlog receives the released vertical space.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\B_009_running_agents_visibility.md:3:title: running-agents indicator misses action and onState runs\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\B_009_running_agents_visibility.md:15:Only some conversation paths register in the global running list. Manual, state-triggered, scheduled, command, agent, and continuation runs can therefore disagree across the shell indicator, card, popup, and conversation panel.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\B_009_running_agents_visibility.md:27:- Starting any action increments the global running count until Electron reports a terminal execution state.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\B_009_running_agents_visibility.md:35:- `design\\architecture\\initial description\\writings\\running_actions.md`\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\F_96_ctrl_enter_on_action_input.md:23:- Prevent default behavior and stop propagation, then flush the latest prompt before running the existing shortcut callback.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\F_165_improve_agent_selectors_on_action_popup.md:5:title: Improve agent selectors on action popup\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\F_165_improve_agent_selectors_on_action_popup.md:32:The selector row appears above agent conversation content. `ActionPopupBottomRow` separately renders the usage controls on the left and run controls on the right. Settings already persist through `ActionRunSettingsStore`; selectors stay disabled while settings load or a run is queued or running, but remain editable while an agent waits for input.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\F_165_improve_agent_selectors_on_action_popup.md:37:- Remove selector rendering from `ActionPopupContent`. Render it only for agent actions in `ActionPopupBottomRow`, before the centered usage group. Lay out selectors left, the existing `tokens`, `changes`, and `lines` controls centered as one group, and run controls right. Keep all groups usable without horizontal overflow when popup width is constrained.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\F_165_improve_agent_selectors_on_action_popup.md:40:- Keep selectors disabled while settings load or run status is `queued` or `running`. Keep them enabled during `waitingForInput`; changes then retain `settingsChangedWhileWaiting` so next send applies restarted settings.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\F_165_improve_agent_selectors_on_action_popup.md:46:- Agent action popup bottom row shows model selector first on left, usage controls centered, and action buttons on right; selector no longer appears above conversation content.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\F_165_improve_agent_selectors_on_action_popup.md:50:- Selectors cannot change while settings load or run is queued or running, but can change while agent waits for input.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\F_164_card_popups_should_behave_like_action_popups.md:5:title: card popups should behave like action popups\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\F_164_card_popups_should_behave_like_action_popups.md:26:Card action popups differ. `CardActionPopupService` stores one stable entry per open popup, `CardActionPopupHost` renders all entries, and `ResizablePopper` supports dragging, eight-direction resizing, persisted desktop size, and activation by pointer or keyboard focus. Entry order supplies `stackPosition`; highest position means top popup.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\F_164_card_popups_should_behave_like_action_popups.md:33:- Keep one entry per card and popup kind. Opening action popup follows current toggle behavior. Opening already-open card-details popup closes it; opening another card adds a second entry instead of replacing first.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\F_164_card_popups_should_behave_like_action_popups.md:34:- Give card-details entries card internal ID, current path, anchor plus fallback anchor, and their own diff selection. Update matching paths after card rename. Card deletion closes only matching card-details entry. Project change clears all entries; leaving board view closes card-details entries without closing action popups.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\F_164_card_popups_should_behave_like_action_popups.md:44:- Desktop can keep multiple card-details popups open, including while multiple card action popups remain open.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\F_164_card_popups_should_behave_like_action_popups.md:46:- Clicking, focusing, dragging, or resizing any card or action popup brings that popup above every other managed popup. Activation does not close, remount, move, or reset another popup.\ndesign\\releases\\0_2_0\\F_164_card_popups_should_behave_like_action_popups.md:49:- Card rename keeps matching popup open on new path. Project change clears all managed popups; leaving board view closes card-details popups while preserving action popups.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\B_005_system_agent_option.md:14:Still present after the F-033 agent-profile rework (2026-07-06 audit). The built-in profile list (`BUILTIN_AGENT_PROFILES` in `app/src/data/agent_profiles.ts` and its duplicate `desktop/agent_profiles.js`) contains `{ command: 'system', name: 'system' }`, and `buildAgentCommand`/`resolveAgentCommand` use the profile's `command` verbatim as the shell command. Selecting the `system` profile (app menu, action popup, action json or `desktop.agent` config) spawns a process literally named `system`, which fails — there is still no mapping to any real default agent.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\B_005_system_agent_option.md:19:* Add validation feedback in the action popup when an agent run fails to spawn (verify spawn `error` events reach the run log/status shown in the popup).\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_2\\B_005_system_agent_option.md:25:* A bad agent command produces a clear failed-run message in the action popup.\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\F_94_no_prefill_prompt_running_conv.md:5:title: no prefill prompt running conv\ndesign\\releases\\0_0_4\\F_94_no_prefill_prompt_running_conv.md:14:When an agent is waiting for a response, but the action popup was closed or on the wrong 'action', then when the user clicks on the action to view the conversation and answer, the input box is p